      "author": "Akash Shelke",
      "rating": 4,
      "text": "Really nice place to spend time with friends...banmaska and chai is too tasty...even sandwich is tasty...just a problem of parking...two wheelers have limited parking..no parking space for four wheelers...over the time period...they did no change at all...kept all as it is...I think they need renovation\nRenovation is done now\n\nCafe Goodluck is an iconic, vintage Irani-style eatery located at the intersection of Ferguson College Road and Bhandarkar Road (Goodluck Chowk) in Deccan Gymkhana, Pune. Established in 1932, it is celebrated as one of the oldest cafes in the city, known for its quick service, pocket-friendly menu, and signature Irani chai.\n\nTimings: Open daily from 8:00 AM to 11:30 PM.Cost Range: Pocket-friendly, generally ₹1 to ₹200 per person.\nCrowd & Vibe: Casual, historic, and h",
      "date": "2026-08-14T16:30:42.622Z",
      "likes": 0
